Package: dictate-uinput
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Javier Santacruz <javier.santacruz.lc@gmail.com>
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Enhances: dictate
Homepage: https://github.com/jvrsantacruz/dictate
Description: let the user at the seat type through /dev/uinput, for dictate
 A udev rule that tags /dev/uinput for uaccess, so logind gives the user
 logged in at the seat write access to it. The paste and type methods of
 dictate press keys through ydotool, which needs that access.
 .
 This package is the whole of the grant, so installing it is the choice to
 make it. The access holds across a user switch: a virtual keyboard opened
 under it keeps working in the next session. Where uinput is a kernel
 module rather than built in, the grant takes effect at the next boot; Ubuntu
 builds it in.
